/** What each update brought, the newest first (the Changelog tab). */
val CHANGELOG: String = listOf(
    "# Changelog",
    "",
    "What's new in each update of Radon Player, the newest at the top. Everything the app does is in **Features**.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.9 · November 2026",
    "- **Update works in Radon Player Next:** the test app's Update fetched the release's APK, which is the other app (Radon Player, not Radon Player Next), so Android refused it (INSTALL_FAILED_INVALID_APK, package inconsistent). Radon Player Next now updates to the newest Next build whenever a new release is out.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.8 · November 2026",
    "- **The DJ keeps DJing when you skip:** a skip near the end of the DJ's queue set off ∞ (Autoplay), which filled the queue with a radio of streams: songs that aren't the DJ's (no sets, so it went quiet), and not only yours. With the DJ on, ∞'s radio never starts now: skip to the end of its queue and it goes on to its next set (waiting for it if it's still picking), and introduces it as always.",
    "- **Only my songs means only yours:** with the DJ's Only my songs on, every set is your songs alone (a stream it found never gets in), and asking for something that isn't in your music finds nothing rather than playing it from everywhere.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.7 · November 2026",
    "- **Covers stay put on the phone:** WAVs are tagged on the phone the way the PC does it (by hand: their ID3 chunk, where the cover is, and LIST INFO, every other chunk kept), not through the tag library, which could read only a WAV's LIST INFO and write it back without its ID3 chunk, cover and all. Any other file whose cover the tag library drops while its other tags change gets it put straight back.",
    "- **Unreleased songs keep their covers:** the phone read the cover inside FLACs only, so to Tags & covers match every MP3, M4A and WAV there looked as if it had none, and each sync wrote the PC's cover into it through the tag library (which could leave it with none at all). The phone now reads the cover in any file, a song that has one is never given another, and a folder named Unreleased is always left alone by a sync, on both devices, whether it's in Folders sync leaves alone or not.",
    "- **Filled-in tags are left alone:** Tags & covers match only fills in what a song is missing now (a tag with nothing in it, a cover when it has none); it never changes a tag that's filled in or replaces a cover. Tags change only when you edit them (the Tagger, Edit tags) or run a scan to change them. The genres the app looks up for its downloads with none aren't sent to your other device either.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.6 · November 2026",
    "- **Presets in pictures:** each Personalization preset shows what it looks like: Now playing (its look, effects and visualizers), a slide of Wrapped in its style and its lyrics card. Tap one in the menu (click on the PC) to see its pictures and swipe through them, then tap it again to put it on; on the PC they also show beside the menu as you point at one, and turn by themselves.",
    "- **Personalization Preset Shuffle:** a switch at the very top of Settings › Personalization puts on a different one of your favourite presets (★) every 5, 10, 15 or 30 minutes (Change every). It only shuffles favourites.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.5 · November 2026",
    "- **30 ready-made Personalization presets:** each a whole setup that goes together, in one tap: a look and theme, a layout, effects, Now playing's visualizer (Dual: one in the middle and one along the bottom) and its colour, Wrapped's style and a lyrics card style to match. Midnight drive, Northern lights, Golden hour, Cherry blossom, Deep ocean, Misty woods, Desert mirage, Old TV, Code rain, Cotton candy, Thunderstorm, First snow, Galaxy quest, Lava lamp, Notebook, Comic book, Vaporwave, Firefly meadow, Love letter, Concert night, Circuit, Autumn walk, Moonlight, Hyperspace, Cabin fire, Polka pop, Neon frame, Contours, Meteor night and Dream orbs.",
    "- **Yours marked:** the presets you saved show (yours) in the Personalization presets menu, so the ready-made ones and yours are easy to tell apart. Presets now keep the visualizer's colour too.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.4 · November 2026",
    "- **No made-up moods:** a song gets moods only from Scan moods, its file's MOOD tag, your own picks or your other device; the guess from the genre alone is gone. After Remove all moods the Moods tab is really empty until you scan (the genre guesses made it look as if moods were still in the files).",
    "- **Dual on Now playing:** Now playing's visualizer button has a Dual switch: pick one style for the middle (around the cover) and one for the bottom, and both play at once, no need to make your own. It's in Settings › Personalization too.",
    "- **Wrapped and lyrics card styles in Personalization:** Settings › Personalization has Wrapped style and Lyrics card style menus (they stay in Wrapped and the Lyrics card box too), so everything about how the app looks is in one place, and a Personalization preset now keeps the Dual visualizer, Wrapped's style and the lyrics card's style as well.",
    "- **Pine forest fixed:** the trees all stand on the bottom edge now (the back row used to float above it), each one solid tree of three tiers on a short trunk (no darker patches where the tiers overlap), sized to the space (no wall of trees in a small preview), and the effect takes its own colour when you pick one.",
    "- **All your personalization in backups and Sync:** your own looks, layouts, visualizers and colour blends, Wrapped styles, lyrics card styles, Personalization presets and now your saved colours too are all in backups, and each Sync adds the other device's to yours (one deleted on either is gone from both). Each device still wears its own look, theme and layout; pick a preset to put the same setup on the other one.",
    "- **One mood scan:** Scan moods, Full scan and Read moods from lyrics are one scan now. Scan moods hears each song whole and reads its words (by the AI when it's on), and only once both are done writes the song's moods (and its words' reading) into its file, so the sound always has its say before anything is written.",
    "- **Moods go into the files only from the scan:** the Write moods into the files tick is gone; nothing writes moods into your files but Scan moods (and moods you pick yourself in the Tagger).",
    "- **Scanned once:** the app keeps track of every song it has scanned and never scans it again; Settings › Reset mood and lyrics scans is the only way to start over. A song whose moods aren't in its file yet (the playing song, moods from your other device) just has them written by the next scan, with nothing heard again.",
    "- **Settings resets for the one scan:** Reset moods works the moods out again from what was heard and read (nothing heard again) and the next Scan moods writes them in; Reset sound scan and Remove all moods are followed by Scan moods too.",
    "",
    "## 3.2.3 · November 2026",
    "- **Artist pictures in Search:** artists found in Search show the same picture as on the Artists tab (the one you picked, or the one looked up), and the ones not looked up yet are looked up there.",
    "- **Lyrics card styles:** the Lyrics card box has a Style menu (by Save and the share buttons): Your look (as before), Now playing (the card as the Now playing screen looks with the Now playing look, in the cover's colours, whatever look is in use), 30 ready-made styles (Synthwave, Aurora night, Golden hour, Cherry blossom, Ocean deep, Old TV, Code rain, Galaxy, Comic book, Hyperspace and more), each with its own colours and effects, and the ones you make. Hold one or tap its ⋯ (right-click on the PC) to favourite it; yours can be edited or deleted there too. The one you pick stays for the next card.",
    "- **Make your own lyrics card:** Settings › Personalization › Make your own › New lyrics card: every colour (the background's top and bottom, the card behind the words, the words, the song name, the soft text, the Radon Player mark), how see-through the card is and its corners, bold or regular words and their size, a round cover, stars and any effects each in its own colour. Start from any ready-made style, Copy my look, Randomize, Randomize colours and Saved colours work there too, and the card shows as you go. Yours go to your other device at each Sync and into backups.",
    "- **Lyrics card with the Now playing look:** the card now looks like the Lyrics screen does with the Now playing look: black, the words in the cover's colour, with the stars and effects (they were left off).",
    "- **Dual volume:** a switch under the Equalizer's Boost (the same screen from Now playing). On (as before): a song with its own volume (Volume… in its menu) gets the Boost on top too. Off: a song with its own volume plays at just that volume, without the Boost; every other song keeps the Boost.",
    "- **Personalization presets:** Settings › Personalization has a Personalization presets menu and a Save as a preset button: it saves everything picked on the tab (look, theme, layout, the looks' own effects or the effects you picked and their colours, Now playing's visualizer) under a name, and picking a preset puts all of it back at once. Hold one or tap its ⋯ (right-click on the PC) to favourite, edit or delete it; Edit puts it on so you can change anything, then Save changes (or Save as new). Presets go to your other device at each Sync and into backups.",
    "- **Mood scans only when you tap them:** Scan moods no longer starts by itself after your music is scanned (or after a sync); Scan moods, Full scan and Read moods from lyrics each run only when you tap them. Moods already in your files are still noticed straight away.",
    "- **Remove all moods takes every one out:** each file is read again after its mood is taken off, and any mood still there (an MP3 tag with an extended header, an M4A's mood saved under another app's name, a FLAC with an ID3 tag in front, a file the usual writer couldn't replace) is blanked where it is, every other tag and the sound kept byte for byte. Files that still keep one are named in Settings › Problems, and moods from your other device wait until a Full scan has heard the songs here again, so a sync can't put the old ones back.",
    "- **Your own Wrapped:** Make your own › New Wrapped: pick its background, text, soft text and accent colours and a colour for each slide, the glow (and how strong), neon text, bold or light type, text size, spacing, corners, round covers and their size, bar thickness, tiles, and stars and effects behind every slide (each effect in its own colour). Randomize, Randomize colours and Saved colours work there too, and a slide in it shows as you go.",
    "- **Wrapped in your look:** Wrapped's Style menu has Your look: the slides take the app's look in use, its stars and effects too.",
